  "term": "Kiddie Schedule for Affective Disorders and Schizophrenia",
  "definition": "The Kiddie Schedule for Affective Disorders and Schizophrenia is a semi-structured clinical interview commonly used in child and adolescent psychiatric research to assess mental disorders in young people. The present and lifetime version has been updated to match DSM-5 categories and is described in the source as showing good validity and inter-rater reliability for clinical research use.",
